      "updated": 1788926400748,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. interface can inherit properties of another interface and\nkeyword used is extends .\n\n2. Multiple inheritance is allowed in interfaces .\n\n\nNew features of interfaces \n=========================\n\n1. even in new interface variables are by default public static\nand final .\n\n2. However it has some new rules regarding methods . An\ninteface can have 3 types of methods .\n\na. abstract methods --> all methods are by default abstract\nand has no body and must be compulsorily inherited by child\nclass or interface .\n\nb. default method - method which are declared default in\ninterface may or may not be inherited by child class or\ninterface. Body is compulsory .\n\nc. static methods --> static methods in interface cannot be\noverriden by child class methods . Body is compulsory . They\ncan only be called by interface name .\n\nd. Private Methods \n\n* Interface can have **private methods** (Java 9+).\n* Private methods **must have a body**.\n* They can be accessed **only inside the same interface**.\n* They are **not inherited** and **cannot be overridden**.\n* They are mainly used as **helper methods** for `default`\nand `static` methods.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. interface can inherit properties of another interface and keyword used is extends .\n\n2. Multiple inheritance is allowed in interfaces .\n\n\nNew features of interfaces \n=========================\n\n1. even in new interface variables are by default public static and final .\n\n2. However it has some new rules regarding methods . An inteface can have 3 types of methods .\n\na. abstract methods --> all methods are by default abstract and has no body and must be compulsorily inherited by child class or interface .\n\nb. default method - method which are declared default in interface may or may not be inherited by child class or interface. Body is compulsory .\n\nc. static methods --> static methods in interface cannot be overriden by child class methods . Body is compulsory . They can only be called by interface name .\n\nd. Private Methods \n\n* Interface can have **private methods** (Java 9+).\n* Private methods **must have a body**.\n* They can be accessed **only inside the same interface**.\n* They are **not inherited** and **cannot be overridden**.\n* They are mainly used as **helper methods** for `default` and `static` methods.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
